{# Demonstrating template for the [diagram] shortcode (Feature f161g).

   Theme developers can include this partial to render a sample
   diagram alongside written documentation, or to verify that the
   theme's CSS targets the .diagram-wrapper / .diagram-caption
   classes the shortcode produces.

   Usage in another template:
       {% include "partials/diagram-example.html.jinja" %}

   The partial expects no template variables; it relies on the
   shortcode preprocessor to expand the [diagram ...]…[/diagram]
   markup into the inline-SVG output documented in
   site-docs/content/04.docs/v0.19/04.markdown-guide/01.diagrams. #}

<section class="diagram-example">
  <h3>Diagram shortcode example</h3>
  <p>
    The <code>[diagram]</code> shortcode renders Mermaid (and future
    Svgbob / plugin) diagrams server-side. Use it for diagrams that
    need a caption, accessible alt text, or an external source file:
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-markdown">[diagram type="mermaid" caption="Build flow" alt="A simple flowchart"]
flowchart LR
  A --&gt; B
  B --&gt; C
[/diagram]</code></pre>
  <p>
    Output is wrapped in <code>&lt;figure
    class="diagram-wrapper diagram-wrapper--mermaid"&gt;</code> with a
    <code>&lt;figcaption&gt;</code>; without caption / alt it falls
    back to a bare <code>&lt;div class="diagram-wrapper"&gt;</code>.
  </p>
</section>
